This is a working-document workflow, not an installed skill.

- Current project state is in control/state.md; assignments and write scopes are
  in control/role_assignments.yaml. The coordinator alone edits control/.
- Read the complete current statement and relevant attachments. Current official
  requirements outrank historical examples and generic templates.
- Use only your assigned write paths. Inputs/raw sources and closed runs are
  immutable. Propose cross-role changes through a versioned handoff.
- Distinguish source facts, assumptions, computed results and interpretations.
  Every important choice needs a problem-specific reason and a meaningful check.
- Preserve a simple defensible baseline. Complexity needs evidence of benefit.
- Numerical claims and figures must trace to accepted data/model/run versions.
- Reviewers do not repair their review targets. State review scope honestly.
- On restart, read current state, assignment and last handoff; do not rely only
  on chat memory. Shared files do not mean shared conversation context.
- This file describes responsibilities, not tool or OS permission enforcement.
- Record AI use as required by the current competition. Do not publish current
  contest work or involve people/services outside the allowed team boundary.
- Do not create remotes, push, install plugins, change user settings or enable
  native teams unless that action is authorized in the current user session.
